# Provider secrets (goal:g1.8). `.env.example` is the committed SHAPE and is
# graph content; `.env` is the value and stays on the box that typed it.
# The negation is defensive: the pattern above is exact today, but anyone who
# widens it to `.env*` in a hurry would otherwise untrack the template too,
# and the graph would lose the one half of this pair it is supposed to hold.
.env
# The swap file the documented one-liner for setting a secret renames
# into place. It exists for milliseconds, and it holds the value while
# it does -- so it is ignored explicitly rather than relying on nobody
# running `git status` inside that window.
.env.swap
!.env.example

.gitnexus
.graph_cache.pkl
.gitnexus_cache.json
loop.log
pi-agi.log
